== Limits ==
* Vague requests give vague results — say what "done" looks like.
* It will not type your passwords or log in for you.
* No OS sandbox on Desktop: commands run with your own user rights and can reach beyond the opened folder.
* It cannot promise perfect code; a green build is evidence about the build, not about everything else.
* Answers depend on which model the session is using.
* Free hours are limited per day; heavy use runs into the allowance.
* Plan and Build are cleanly separated on Desktop; the CLI behaviour differs, so check your installed version.
* A Cloud chat works on a copy of the project, not your local folder — merging is yours, through git.

== FAQ ==
; Do I need to know programming?
: No, but it helps. You need to say clearly what you want and check the result.

; Is it really free?
: Yes — ads pay for the models, and there is no card or API key required. Paid plans exist for more model time.

; Can it break my project?
: It can make mistakes. Use Plan mode first for big changes and keep the project in git.

; Where does my code go?
: On Desktop it stays in the folder you opened. On Cloud it runs in a cloud workspace for that project.

; Can I choose the model?
: Yes, the model picker shows each model and how many hours an hour on it costs. To see it, turn on advanced composer in general settings

; What is "Freebucks"?
: The older credit unit. Balances are shown in hours now; 1 hour = 5 Freebucks.

; Does it train on my code?
: Only when a model or feature says data may be used for training. Check that notice per model.

== Glossary ==
; Agent
: The AI that does the work, not just answers questions. Here its name is Buffy.
; Prompt
: The message you type to ask for something.
; Repo (repository)
: A project folder tracked by git, so changes can be reviewed or undone.
; Terminal
: The text window where commands are typed. Freebuff can use it for you.
; Build
: Turning source code into something that runs, and checking that it does.
; Sandbox / workspace
: A separate place where the project runs. Cloud has one; Desktop does not isolate your OS.
; Mode
: How much power the agent has: Plan (read only) or Build (can change files).
; Subagent
: A helper agent given one narrow job, whose result goes back to the main agent.
; Referral link
: A link that credits whoever shared it when a new user signs up.

